Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: rmac (Lulo OS)
Source: https://github.com/millionrust/lulo
Comment:
 This source package is made from one exact commit of the repository, named
 in debian/changelog and debian/rmac-revision: rmac_*.orig.tar.xz is the
 `git archive` export of that commit, and rmac_*.orig-vendor.tar.xz holds the
 Rust crates that `cargo vendor --locked` fetched for the commit's two
 Cargo.lock files (Cargo.lock and shell/Cargo.lock). It builds the rmac-apps
 and rmac-session binary packages.
 .
 The binaries statically link the Rust crates in vendor/. Every vendored
 crate's declared licence and its licence and notice files are reproduced in
 debian/dependency-licenses.txt, generated from vendor/ when the source
 package is made. Some vendored crates only build for other platforms and
 are not linked in. The repository's dependency policy (deny.toml,
 shell/deny.toml) lists the licences a dependency may use.
 .
 The rmac-apps and rmac-session binary packages carry the MIT licence below as
 /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright; rmac-apps also carries LICENSES.md, the
 inventory of its original desktop metadata and artwork.

